<title>GREECE: GREEK RETAIL SALES RISE 6.2 PCT YR/YR IN FEBRUARY.</title>
<headline>GREEK RETAIL SALES RISE 6.2 PCT YR/YR IN FEBRUARY.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's retail sales (turnover)</p>
<p>rose 6.2 percent year-on-year in February from 10.7 percent in</p>
<p>January, the National Statistics Service (NSS) said in a</p>
<p>statement.</p>
<p>Foodstuffs increased 1.8 percent, apparel and footwear 1.7</p>
<p>percent, furniture and household goods 16.5 percent and</p>
<p>miscellaneous 9.7 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Average sales were up 8.5 percent year-on-year in the period</p>
<p>January-February 1997.</p>
<p>    Retail sales		  Feb 97   Jan 97   Feb 96</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		    6.2%    10.7%	 9.4%</p>
<p>    Index (1988=100)	     247.1    240.6     232.7</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
